                  "explanation": "Source-visible behavior: at notes-post, the action declares PaperlessNotePermissions, the supplied global permissions satisfy the POST permission map, and the handler's POST-specific change_document gate uses owner-aware logic. In the current other-present case, the caller's stated object change_document grant makes that gate pass, so note creation is reachable. The absent-owner counterfactual also reaches creation because the visible helper permits an ownerless object. Policy comparison: the current and absent branches both satisfy the stated rule through the change_document grant or ownerless/owner-eligible source condition; the accepted policy otherwise requires global permissions plus ownership or an object change_document grant. The later note-store or search operations are not needed to decide authorization; any source-external store failure is not authorization.",
